Changelog
---------

1.0 (Unreleased)
````````````````
* Ensure mock package gets installed on testing.

0.9 (2014-08-02)
````````````````
* First beta release
* Sphinx documentation available on Read The Docs
* Fix compatability between extension and convert decorators

0.8 (2014-03-13)
````````````````
* Boolean flags create both '--opt' and '--no-opt' command line options
* Replace '_' with '-' in command line option flags
* Enable creating sub-commands with a specified name
* Custom help formatters for control command line help output
* Create positional command line arguments for required parameters
* Published Python wheel packages to PyPI to improve install times
* Deprecate context.return_value for context.last_return and
  context.return_values

0.7.1 (2013-10-03)
``````````````````
* Fix incompatability between automatic type conversion and command line flags

0.7 (2013-10-01)
````````````````
* New utility functions tofile and tolist
* Fix bug prevent help output with main function that takes on arguments
* Multiple subcommands support can be enabled with cmd_delim
* Context object available to main and subcommand functions for storing state
* Optional automatic type conversion for begin.convert and begin.start
* Command line flags for options with boolean default values

0.6 (2013-08-27)
````````````````
* Allow listing of optins in alphabetical order
* Allow suppression of short options

0.5 (2013-08-01)
````````````````
* Add support for sub-commands, sub-command groups and entry points

0.4 (2013-07-20)
````````````````
* Add function decorators to extend command line options to:
   * Configure the logging module
   * Configrue the tracebacks module
* Support configuration files to set defaults for command line options

0.3 (2013-07-10)
````````````````
* Depend on external funcsigs package for Python earlier than 3.3
* Depend on external argparse package for Python 2.6
* Use argparse instead over optparse internally for command line processing

0.2 (2013-07-04)
````````````````
* Fix missing begin.funcsigs package in source distribution

0.1 (2013-03-24)
````````````````
* First version released
* begin.start() decorator
* begin.convert() decorator


1.0.0 (2026-11-10)
------------------

First modern release of the trollkarlen fork.

- Python 3.11+ only (3.10 and older are end-of-life). Supports 3.11-3.15.
- Compatibility with current setuptools and Python 3.12/3.13/3.14/3.15:
  - pkg_resources (removed from setuptools 81) replaced with
    importlib.metadata in subcommand plugin loading.
  - distutils.util.strtobool (removed with distutils in 3.12) replaced
    with a local implementation in begin.utils.
  - cgitb (removed in 3.13, PEP 594): the tracebacks extension now falls
    back to a plain sys.excepthook writing text tracebacks to stderr and
    --tbdir, matching cgitb's logdir behaviour.
  - Restored begin.utils.tolist (referenced by convert's automatic
    list/tuple casting and its tests, but lost from the module years
    ago).
- Packaging: setup.py/travis/tox replaced by pyproject.toml (hatchling
  backend) usable with uv; version sourced from begin/version.py.
- Quality gates wired into pyproject and CI (GitHub Actions):
  ruff, black, pylint (10.00/10), mypy, pytest with coverage
  (131 tests, 98% coverage, gate at 80%), matrix 3.11-3.15 on official
  interpreters.
- Test suite repaired for modern Python (cgitb/pkg_resources mocks,
  unittest2/funcsigs/py2 fallbacks removed) and extended: cgitb-free
  traceback fallback, utils edge cases. test_automatic_list restored to
  its original 2013 intent (mutable list default) after a 2014 lint
  "fix" had silently invalidated it.
- All inline lint suppressions carry a reason; project-wide patterns
  (argparse internals access, dynamically-created context attributes)
  are disabled in the pylint config with justification.
